# rodeo-cli

Terraform-style CLI for nested KVM labs on SLES 16 (bare-metal or Instruqt).
`rodeo up` ≈ `terraform apply`: declarative plan → phase pipeline → idempotent convergence.

GitHub: https://github.com/avaleror/rodeo-cli
Authors: Andres Valero (avaleror), Raúl Mahiques — SUSE

## Two-dimension model

- **Platform** (`type:`): what to deploy — `rodeo/profiles/<name>.py` + `rodeo/data/platforms/<name>/definition.yaml`
- **Host context** (`deployment_target:`): `baremetal` | `instruqt` — guards phases, DNAT, external IP, success output

Bundled platforms: `suse-virt`, `rancher`, `suse-edge`.

## Phase pipeline

```
kvm_host → vms → [pxe_server → cluster] → [rancher] → finalise
```

`deployment_target: instruqt` skips `finalise` pre-snapshot.

## Reuse before inventing

| Need | Location |
|------|----------|
| Root / tmux | `rodeo/privilege.py` |
| Deploy pipeline | `rodeo/commands/deploy.py:execute_deploy()` |
| Secrets / lab dir | `rodeo/config.py` |
| Host detect | `rodeo/preflight.py:detect_host()` |
| Secret files | `rodeo/secretgen.py` |
| Instruqt detect | `rodeo/commands/up_cmd.py:_detect_target()` |

New shared helpers go in those modules — not inlined in commands.

Describe the tool as "Terraform-style" or "phase-based". Never mention kcli.
